---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How the Quilt Fabric Planner Works — QuiltClarity"
  description="See how QuiltClarity combines a cut list, real fabric stock, fresh-fabric comparison, purchase shortfall, and one executable cutting plan."
>
  <article class="page article-page">
    <header class="hero compact-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p><h1>
        From an existing cut list to one fabric plan
      </h1><p class="lede">
        QuiltClarity starts after you already know the rectangular pieces your
        pattern or project requires.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="article-body">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Enter the cuts and fabrics</h2><p>
          Add each required rectangle, assign its fabric, and identify finished
          or cut dimensions. Piece-level direction and WOF restrictions stay
          explicit.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>2. Describe fabric you already own</h2><p>
          Enter each remnant, fat quarter, or partial yard as a physical
          width-by-length rectangle. Edited dimensions, not preset names,
          control placement.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>3. Compare and reconcile</h2><p>
          The planner compares any pattern-stated amount with an independent
          fresh-fabric plan, then jointly evaluates stock and the raw additional
          bolt length. Safety and shop rounding apply only to new fabric.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>4. Execute the selected plan</h2><p>
          The shopping list, stock allocations, purchased layout, instructions,
          SVG diagrams, and leftover regions all come from the same selected
          placements. The bounded practical heuristic is deterministic but is
          not claimed to prove a global minimum.
        </p>
      </section>
      <p>
        <a class="button" href="/fabric-cutting-planner/"
          >Open the project fabric planner</a
        >
      </p>
      <p>
        Review the <a href="/methodology/">calculation methodology</a> or browse the{
          ' '
        }
        <a href="/guides/">measurement guides</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
